im]`sase ace` startup returns to at or below its 2026-08-12 baseline [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim](median `visible_ready` <= 2.8 s, `agents_ready` <= 3.4 s), monitor[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]reconciliation no longer runs synchronously inside the agents disk [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]load, and an operation-count regression gate keeps data-scaled work[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]off the startup path.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]5[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]3[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202608/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]tui_startup_monitor_reconcile.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202608/tui_startup_monitor_reconcile.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-n7[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-n7/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Reorder the reconcile guards[/bold #D7AFFF]                                  [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]guards[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]guards: reorder `should_reconcile_dead_supervisor` so the cheap [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]`monitor_state`/`pid` rejects run before `proc_shell_owns()`, which [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]currently does a full proc-store read for all 147 records when 0 survive[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the next two lines; add a test asserting the proc lookup is skipped for [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]terminal and pid-less records. Measured saving 1.47 s.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Kill the N+1 proc-store reads[/bold #D7AFFF]                                 [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]snapshot[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]snapshot: add a snapshot-scoped proc lookup so `get_proc` stops [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]re-reading and re-parsing the whole store per id, thread one snapshot [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]through the reconcile pass and `_with_proc_projection`, and test that [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]proc-store reads stay bounded regardless of record count.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Stop the O(archive) index query[/bold #D7AFFF]                               [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]bounded-query[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]bounded-query: give reconciliation its own bounded artifact-index query [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]instead of the unbounded full-history `include_hidden` scan of the 115 [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]MB index, leave the `list_monitors` listing path unchanged, and pin the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]new bounds with a test. Escalate to the Rust core if the predicate is [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]not expressible in the existing wire query.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Take reconciliation off the synchronous load[/bold #D7AFFF]                  [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]off-read-path[dim] · [dim][/dim]after guards, snapshot, bounded-query[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]off-read-path: remove the synchronous [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]`_reconcile_dead_monitor_supervisors_for_tui()` call from [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]`_load_agents_from_disk_impl` and run it in the background with a [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]coalesced follow-up refresh, reusing the existing loader-cleanup shape, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]while preserving settlement semantics and preventing overlapping passes.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Pin the win with a regression gate[/bold #D7AFFF]                            [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]gate[dim] · [dim][/dim]after off-read-path[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]gate: add a `tests/perf/` bench and baseline asserting bounded [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]proc-store reads and index queries per disk load and no synchronous [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]reconciliation, preferring deterministic operation counts over [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]wall-clock seconds, and ask the user before recording the incident in [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the tui_perf memory note.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-n7","llm_provider":"claude","model":"sonnet","patch_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","phase_bead_id":"sase-n7.1","reasoning_effort":"high","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},"source_run_id":"run-04b770c7553aa4a6690bd56963a267b7","started_at":"2026-08-16T15:21:27.823692+00:00","state":"completed"},{"commits":[],"dismissed_at":null,"files":{"commits":{"digest":"aa0064a9207867ab30dae1e650ff708ccdc61b374a511b83ad9ea97117a36d6f","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-n7.2/commits.json","size_bytes":89},"embedded_workflows":{"digest":"a398c70160fe308637edd70b38d8cf02cc697183c480675d10f387d529663058","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-n7.2/embedded_workflows.json","size_bytes":80},"meta":{"digest":"3e5f6dccbd2540cccb23158e7518dfae0823a851f5b520beca0af7446871b121","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-n7.2/meta.json","size_bytes":633},"prompt":{"digest":"c399d8081d4c42e6c02201aee3631db3e01ebf7dc690bef16380c44d4b3f73af","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-n7.2/prompt.md","size_bytes":109},"prompt_steps":{"digest":"d22c9562ea4dd379f9139b9748da7c22ff10f2a4fc1a25eea4223f06130413e3","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-n7.2/prompt_steps.json","size_bytes":4113},"state":{"digest":"03ae4d23b794f9d1c4b0e2a1b35572c288b67343eb228f1959a8dbd6c8f3e05d","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-n7.2/state.json","size_bytes":180}},"finished_at":null,"global_name":"bbugyi200.athena.sase-n7.2","local_name":"sase-